WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.250
Why does Microsoft 365 need its own gate?

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:08.062
In the admin center, each administrator's
view of the Message center is their own.

3
00:00:08.062 --> 00:00:12.249
Archiving a post removes it only
from that administrator's view,

4
00:00:12.249 --> 00:00:17.462
and the weekly digest goes, by default, to
each administrator's own primary email.

5
00:00:17.462 --> 00:00:22.319
Microsoft gives at least thirty days'
notice of a major update that needs action,

6
00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:25.263
and the act-by date is
rare enough that Microsoft

7
00:00:25.263 --> 00:00:27.912
says to pay extra
attention when it appears.

8
00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:31.810
So the program reads the posts
from Microsoft Graph instead,

9
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:36.175
through the service communications
A P I, with two read permissions.

10
00:00:36.175 --> 00:00:37.187
There's a trap.

11
00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:41.931
A GCC High tenant read on the
worldwide Graph host returns nothing,

12
00:00:41.931 --> 00:00:44.776
and an empty list looks like a quiet week.

13
00:00:44.776 --> 00:00:47.728
So the kit reads only the
cloud the settings name,

14
00:00:47.728 --> 00:00:51.190
and refuses a session in
another environment or tenant.
